## What is wrong (one paragraph)

In `google.ts`, `exchange()` (line 62) reads the token answer at line 87: `const tokens = (await tokenRes.json()) as { access_token: string; id_token?: string };` and uses `tokens.access_token` at line 90 in `Authorization: Bearer ${tokens.access_token}` with no check. A 200 answer with no `access_token` (empty object, non-string, empty string) therefore reaches Google's userinfo endpoint as `Bearer undefined`, and the sign-in fails there with a profile-fetch error instead of at the token exchange. The fix types the field as `unknown`, refuses a missing, non-string or empty `access_token` with a logged warning (provider name only, never the answer) and an Error `Google token exchange failed (no access token)`, before any profile call. Nothing else changes: the `!tokenRes.ok` branch above (`Google token exchange failed (HTTP <status>)`), the userinfo call, the profile mapping and `exchangeCode`'s timeout/unreachable wrapper stay as they are. A non-timeout Error is rethrown by `exchangeCode` unchanged, so the new message reaches the caller as written.

